  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Ecclesiastes",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 10,
    "summary": "A little folly destroys the reputation of the wise and honorable—The words of a wise man’s mouth are gracious—A fool is full of words.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Dead flies cause the ointment of the apothecary to send forth a stinking savour: so doth a little folly him that is in reputation for wisdom and honour.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 47,
            "text": "OR perfumer (ointment maker)."
          },
          {
            "start": 98,
            "end": 103,
            "text": "Josh. 7:11 (1, 11–12); Eccl. 9:18."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 81,
            "end": 88
          },
          {
            "start": 141,
            "end": 144
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 10:1",
        "book": "Ecclesiastes",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "A wise man’s heart is at his right hand; but a fool’s heart at his left.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 21
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 10:2",
        "book": "Ecclesiastes",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "Yea also, when he that is a fool walketh by the way, his wisdom faileth him, and he saith to every one that he is a fool.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 76
          },
          {
            "start": 103,
            "end": 107
          },
          {
            "start": 111,
            "end": 113
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 10:3",
        "book": "Ecclesiastes",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "If the spirit of the ruler rise up against thee, leave not thy place; for yielding pacifieth great offences.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 10:4",
        "book": "Ecclesiastes",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "There is an evil which I have seen under the sun, as an error which proceedeth from the ruler:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 22
          },
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 67
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 10:5",
        "book": "Ecclesiastes",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "Folly is set in great dignity, and the rich sit in low place.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 10:6",
        "book": "Ecclesiastes",
        "chapter": 10,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "I have seen servants upon horses, and princes walking as servants upon the earth.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "Prov. 19:10."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Prov. 19:10.",
            "prettyString": "Proverbs 19:10",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
